# Gradle dependency lock files are deliberately not ignored: they are the record of
# which versions a build resolves, they are what the Trivy scans read, and Gradle
# itself writes "This file is expected to be part of source control" into them.
#
# The root settings lock file is the exception. The root build declares no locking, so
# running --write-locks anywhere in the composite leaves behind a file whose only entry is
# the version catalog placeholder.
/settings-gradle.lockfile

